  "answer": {
    "report": "I repaired the `PandasDfHandler.restore` method in `jsonpickle/ext/pandas.py` to correctly handle numeric dtype codes.\n\nThe issue was that `np.dtype(dtype_str)` was being called on tags like `pd/i8` or `pd/i`, which are not valid NumPy dtype strings. I modified the dtype application loop to:\n1. Detect tags starting with `pd/`.\n2. Map legacy generic tags without explicit widths (`pd/i`, `pd/u`, `pd/f`, `pd/in`) to their widest counterparts (`int64`, `uint64`, `float64`) to ensure value preservation while allowing widening.\n3. Use `REVERSE_TYPE_MAP` to resolve specific tags (e.g., `pd/i8` $\\rightarrow$ `int8`) to maintain exact dtype widths for both historical and new objects.\n4. Fall back to the original `dtype_str` for non-pandas tags.\n\nI ran the `legacy` check suite, which identified failures in historical artifacts where numeric values were being corrupted or dtypes were incorrectly inferred as `object` or wrong widths due to the `np.dtype` failure.\n\nNo unresolved work remains regarding the specified numeric dtype contract."
  },
